In Prisma 7, the configuration of the database connection URL has moved out of the `schema.prisma` file and into the **`prisma.config.ts`** file and the **`PrismaClient` constructor**[1][2].

The `url` field in the `datasource` block of `schema.prisma` is no longer supported and will trigger error `P1012`[1][3].

### 1. Update `schema.prisma`
Remove the `url` property from your `datasource` block[1][2]:

```prisma
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql" // or "mysql", "sqlite", etc.
  // url = env("DATABASE_URL") // REMOVE THIS LINE
}
```

### 2. Configure `prisma.config.ts`
Create or update your `prisma.config.ts` file in the project root to define your datasource[4][1]:

```typescript
import { defineConfig, env } from 'prisma/config';

export default defineConfig({
  schema: './prisma/schema.prisma',
  datasource: {
    url: env('DATABASE_URL'), // Define the URL here for CLI tools (Migrate, etc.)
  },
});
```

